          <div class="liquid-panel static-panel faq-item overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 rounded-xl">
            <button class="faq-button w-full text-left p-4 sm:p-6 flex justify-between items-center focus:outline-none hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-colors">
              <h3 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-semibold text-white pr-6">Can I use this calculator for crypto and forex?</h3>
              <div class="relative flex-shrink-0 w-6 h-6 flex items-center justify-center bg-white/5 rounded-full border border-white/10">
                 <span class="absolute w-2.5 h-0.5 bg-[var(--theme-accent-blue)] transition-transform duration-300 rounded-full"></span>
                 <span class="absolute w-2.5 h-0.5 bg-[var(--theme-accent-blue)] rotate-90 transition-transform duration-300 faq-vertical-line rounded-full"></span>
              </div>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-300 ease-in-out">
              <div class="overflow-hidden">
                <p class="text-sm text-[var(--theme-text-muted)] leading-relaxed px-4 sm:px-6 pb-4 sm:pb-6 pt-0">
                  Yes. The math behind the Kelly formula is universal. As long as you know your historical win rate and net reward-to-risk ratio, you can use the engine to optimize sizing for stocks, crypto, forex, or any probabilistic event.
                </p>
              </div>
